---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site, spacecamps } from "../data/site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How airpport Pty Ltd collects, uses and protects personal information through this website and when you contact us."
  summary="How we handle personal information when you visit this website or get in touch with us. The short version: this site has no cookies or analytics, and we only hold what you choose to send us."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This policy applies to <strong>{site.legalName}</strong> (ABN {site.abn}, ACN {site.acn}), referred to as
    "airpport", "we", "us" or "our". We are an Australian software company based in New South Wales. We handle
    personal information in line with the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers this website ({site.url.replace("https://", "")}) and any contact you have with airpport
    directly, such as writing to us about our products, partnerships or a business idea.
  </p>
  <p>
    {spacecamps.name} has its own privacy policy, which applies when you use the {spacecamps.name} service or website. You
    can read it at <a href={`${spacecamps.url}/privacy-policy`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">spacecamps.com.au/privacy-policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect personal information you choose to give us. That can include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, email address and business name</li>
    <li>the content of your message, and any details you include in it</li>
    <li>records of our correspondence with you</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use cookies, analytics, advertising pixels or any other tracking. Fonts and images are served
    from this website, so no third-party services are loaded while you browse.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so the site
    remembers it next time. It stays on your device and is never sent to us. You can clear it at any time through your
    browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. in the United States. Like most web hosts, GitHub
    may log technical details of each visit, such as your IP address, for security and to keep the service running. We
    don't receive or use these logs. GitHub's handling of this data is described in the
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub General Privacy Statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <p>We use the information you send us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>reply to your enquiry and keep a record of the conversation</li>
    <li>discuss, provide or improve our products and services</li>
    <li>follow up on partnership or product ideas you've raised with us</li>
    <li>meet our legal, tax and accounting obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We won't add you to a mailing list or send you marketing unless you ask us to, and you can tell us to stop at any
    time. We never sell personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We only share personal information when we need to, with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>service providers who help us run the business, such as our email and file storage providers</li>
    <li>professional advisers, such as our accountant or lawyer</li>
    <li>government bodies or others where the law requires or allows it</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these providers, including GitHub, store data outside Australia, mainly in the United States. When we use
    overseas providers, we take reasonable steps to make sure they protect personal information to a standard
    consistent with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2>How we store and protect it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information in secure, access-controlled systems and take reasonable steps to protect it from
    misuse, loss, and unauthorised access, change or disclosure. We keep it only for as long as we need it for the
    purposes above or as the law requires, then delete or de-identify it.
  </p>

  <h2>Access and correction</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by contacting
    us. We'll respond within 30 days. If we can't do what you ask, we'll explain why.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you're concerned about how we've handled your personal information, contact us and we'll respond within 30
    days. If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner at
    <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The current version is always on this page, with the date it was last
    updated at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName}<br />
    {site.state}, {site.location}
  </p>
  <p>See also our <a href="/terms/">terms and conditions</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
